course: dictionary
lesson: 10063
title: Texan
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: A Texan is a person from Texas, a big state in the south of the USA. As a noun, it names the person: «Ella's cousin is a Texan.» As an adjective, it describes something from or about Texas: «The Texan ranch had horses and miles of grass.»
explain: Look at the words around it to work out which job Texan is doing. If a word comes before a noun, like «Texan ranch» or «Texan accent», it is probably an adjective. If it stands alone as the subject or object, it is probably a noun, as in «Ella met a Texan at the rodeo».
explain: Context can also tell you about the feeling and the people. «Come on over here, boy,» said the Texan grandpa. Boy is his word for a lad, so you can guess the grandpa is friendly. When you are not sure, check your meaning by putting it into the sentence and seeing if it still makes sense.
fact: Texan (noun) means a person from Texas. The plural is Texans.
fact: Texan (adjective) means from or to do with Texas, like a Texan accent.
fact: Texas is a big state in the south of the USA, so maths problems often use it as an example of a very large state.
fact: Texans are linked with ranches, cowboys, oil, barbecue and rodeos.
fact: A Texan accent has a famous drawl, a slow way of stretching out the vowels when people speak.
exercise: «The Texan ranch had horses and miles of grass.» Which state does Texan point to? | Florida | California | Alaska | *Texas
exercise: Ella's cousin lives in Texas. What is her cousin? | A Scot | *A Texan | A cowboy only | A rodeo
exercise: «The Texan grandpa said, "Come here, boy."» What does boy mean here? | A kind of hat | A wooden fence | A sheep | *A lad, a young boy
test: «A Texan accent has a famous drawl.» What part of speech is Texan here? | Verb | *Adjective | Adverb | Noun
test: Where is NASA's mission control? | *Houston, Texas | Ohio | Montana | Hawaii
exam: In which sentence is Texan a noun? | «The Texan ranch was huge.» | «The Texan accent is famous.» | *«A Texan came into town with a hat.» | «Texan barbecue smells great.»
